      "event": "Flash Flood Warning",
      "severity": "Severe",
      "urgency": "Immediate",
      "certainty": "Likely",
      "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued October 29 at 4:38PM HST until October 29 at 5:45PM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
      "description": "At 438 PM HST, Doppler radar indicates decreasing rain rates over\nEast Maui with rain rates of less than one in per hour. The heaviest\nrain continues to occur over far east Maui near Hamoa and Hana. Flash\nflooding is ongoing but conditions should gradually improve over the\nnext hour.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by heavy rain.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nKipahulu, Nahiku, Kaupo, Hana, Keanae, Haleakala National Park,\nWailua, Hamoa and Kailua.",
      "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.",
      "areaDesc": "Maui, HI",
      "zones": [],
      "effective": "2026-10-29T16:38:00-10:00",
