  "outlookText": "000\nACPN50 PHFO 292307\nTWOCP \n\nTropical Weather Outlook\nNWS Central Pacific Hurricane Center Honolulu HI\nIssued by NWS National Hurricane Center Miami FL\n200 PM HST Thu Oct 29 2026\n\nFor the central North Pacific...between 140W and 180W:\n\nActive Systems:\nThe National Hurricane Center is issuing advisories on recently\ndowngraded Tropical Depression Vance, located about one hundred\nmiles southeast of the southern tip of the Baja California\nPeninsula.\n\nWell Southeast of the Hawaiian Islands:\nA broad area of low pressure is likely to develop well to the\nsoutheast of the Hawaiian Islands this weekend or early next week.\nThereafter, environmental conditions appear generally favorable for\nsome slow development of this system as it moves westward to\nwest-northwestward into the Central Pacific basin.\n* Formation chance through 48 hours...low...near 0 percent.\n* Formation chance through 7 days...low...30 percent.\n\n$$\nForecaster Evans/Papin\nNNNN",
